Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: stop a scheduling round when the hardware refuses a frame

ath11k_dp_tx() returns -ENOSPC when the tx descriptor idr is full and
-ENOMEM when the TCL ring has no descriptor left (or a DMA mapping fails).
Both mean the hardware has no room for this frame, and no room for a frame
from any other queue either, so continuing the round only burns CPU and
drops frames that mac80211 has already dequeued.

End the round on those two errors instead. The next tx completion starts a
new one, so nothing has to poll the ring pointer per frame.

This is a backport of patch 8/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index 2f2ce10..0f40b11 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -6229,10 +6229,11 @@ static int ath11k_mac_tx(struct ath11k *ar, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static void ath11k_mac_push_txq(struct ath11k *ar, struct ieee80211_txq *txq)
+static int ath11k_mac_push_txq(struct ath11k *ar, struct ieee80211_txq *txq)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_hw *hw = ar->hw;
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
+	int ret;
 
 	/* The airtime queue limit is checked per frame rather than only at
 	 * selection time: a station whose limit binds mid-selection must stop
@@ -6244,22 +6245,34 @@ static void ath11k_mac_push_txq(struct ath11k *ar, struct ieee80211_txq *txq)
 		if (!skb)
 			break;
 
-		ath11k_mac_tx(ar, txq->sta, skb);
+		ret = ath11k_mac_tx(ar, txq->sta, skb);
+
+		/* Either the tx descriptor idr or the TCL ring is full. The
+		 * remaining queues have nowhere to put a frame either, so end
+		 * the round here; the next tx completion starts a new one.
+		 */
+		if (ret == -ENOSPC || ret == -ENOMEM)
+			return ret;
 	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 void ath11k_mac_tx_push_pending(struct ath11k *ar, u8 ac)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_hw *hw = ar->hw;
 	struct ieee80211_txq *txq;
+	int ret;
 
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	spin_lock_bh(&ar->txq_lock);
 
 	ieee80211_txq_schedule_start(hw, ac);
 	while ((txq = ieee80211_next_txq(hw, ac))) {
-		ath11k_mac_push_txq(ar, txq);
+		ret = ath11k_mac_push_txq(ar, txq);
 		ieee80211_return_txq(hw, txq, false);
+		if (ret)
+			break;
 	}
 	ieee80211_txq_schedule_end(hw, ac);
 
